{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head `55506bef7b991bf5987bcc61d79e25ddee10d284`, on main `0719adce`. This verdict also reviews step 1 under `2082efd9`, which I promised in `986b0da9`. The head changes the note and one section of `docs/security/trust-boundaries.md`, and no source file, so it needs no gate. I reviewed `1eba1153` first, then read the diff to this head.\n\n**Step 1.** Both sealed units verify against their `SHA256SUMS`, and neither holds a writable file.\n\n- Every band in the four client logs carries `allEqual: true`, and each commit in the press text exists in the sealed repositories at `repo`, `repo-change-2` and `repo-change-3`. The other IDs in those texts are blobs or trees, which the page labels.\n- Each new read signs one act: entries 22, 24, 26, 28, 30, 46, 48, 50, 52, 54 and 56. The held reads sign nothing. `read-tokens.json` confirms the acts of the first unit.\n- No token reached a file. The builder's scans show 0 for each session bearer, workspace token, provider shape and key. My own grep for `art_v1_`, `x-access-token` and `ghs_` finds nothing in either unit.\n\n**The person's session.** I pressed the reconstruction, and it holds.\n\n- I read entries 60 to 74 of the destination, with `entries.mts` under the `agent-a` home. The read wrote no entry, and the home's session cache kept its 10:42 time. Entries 60, 70 and 72 are `read-token` acts at the note's three times, signed by `key_eHLaY0`.\n- `key_eHLaY0` appears in the `owner` home, and `key_vxHfcp`, which signed entries 62 to 68, appears in the `agent-a` home. So the note's attribution holds.\n- Each act falls inside one call in the app's log. Id 9 runs from 18:43:46.948Z to 18:43:58.528Z, which is the note's 11.58 s. Id 17 runs from 19:03:49Z to 19:03:56Z. Id 18 runs from 19:17:25Z to 19:17:31Z.\n- `2-diff.png` has the digest that the note gives, and I read its four commit IDs. They equal the table and the sealed repositories.\n- The planner's `353a0ec0` holds the person's 14:20 words.\n\nThe exact-commit clause rests on one screenshot of one band and on one word from a person for the others. The note says so in its open limits, and the acceptance stays with the planner.\n\n**The security section.** The probe's results show the claim on Cloudflare Artifacts: `git ls-remote` lists three staged refs, including the commit's, and `git fetch` returns that commit. The section follows the token section, whose time limits it relies on, and it says where the run took place. Its second sentence states the rule with no host, and no run on GitHub shows it. I do not hold the head for that, because the next sentence names the host of the run. At the next edit, the section can say that no run covers GitHub.\n\n**Architecture.** The record separates what a run showed, what a person said and what the note reconstructs, and it labels each source. It changes no boundary.\n\n**Security.** The section tells a reader more than the token section did: a revoked key's token reaches unmerged work for the token's life. The evidence holds no credential. The note names the fault in `out/client-v1.log`, where entries 22 and 24 say \"another key\", and leaves the sealed files as they are. That is the right repair for sealed files.\n\n**Simplification.** One note and one section, with nothing to remove.\n\n`check-notes`, `check-doc-links` (1003 links, 0 broken) and `check-commit-messages` pass at this head, and the worktree is clean.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d15d70d5bbe255ce9f3ab1f97e809c279ba70f60","binding":"assigned","head":"55506bef7b991bf5987bcc61d79e25ddee10d284","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ad5a011c6944697612e813d7348cc8a1843b3abc\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1e1fd1fecaae7a3b6076a2d0a438a5d1569d6ce2\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ad5a011c69446